WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.632 --> 00:00:02.140
- This is very cozy.

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.584
(cheering)

00:00:04.584 --> 00:00:05.960
I'm short.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.184
- Moving the pillows, I know.

00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:08.587
- I'm really short.

00:00:08.587 --> 00:00:09.420
- I know,

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.360
In my legs, I have no legs.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.450
I am all torso.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:12.370
- I've got nothin'.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.070
So if I don't put 75 pillows,

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.370
I end up sitting like Edith Ann.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.163
I look like that.

00:00:18.163 --> 00:00:19.463
- Was it Lily Tomlin in the big chair.

00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:20.437
- That's Edith Ann, yes.

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:22.145
- Oh is that a character?

00:00:22.145 --> 00:00:23.690
- Every time I sit somewhere I'm like

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.030
pretty sure that's what it looks like.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.096
- I know,

00:00:26.096 --> 00:00:27.010
'cause tall people always
complain about being on planes,

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:27.843
but short people, it sucks,

00:00:27.843 --> 00:00:28.830
'cause you lose your circulation

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.660
'cause your feet don't touch the floor.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:31.860
- It's very difficult for short people

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.103
you tall people.

00:00:33.103 --> 00:00:34.590
- I don't want to hear all
your tall people problems.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.130
You are perfect to host Little Big Shots.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:37.963
(cheering)

00:00:37.963 --> 00:00:38.796
You are.

00:00:38.796 --> 00:00:39.879
It's so cool.

00:00:42.077 --> 00:00:43.077
How did this come about?

00:00:43.077 --> 00:00:45.120
And what are you most
excited about the show?

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.290
- Kind of all of that.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.167
When it first came up I was like,

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.627
"No I shouldn't do that.

00:00:49.627 --> 00:00:50.679
"That seems crazy."

00:00:50.679 --> 00:00:51.830
- That's what I said about this.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:52.663
Watch out.

00:00:52.663 --> 00:00:53.496
- Uh oh.

00:00:53.496 --> 00:00:54.380
- Yeah.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.890
- You do start to feel like,
that's not really what I do.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.880
I don't want to screw it up
for kids, was my main thing.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.410
All these great kids are
coming on and I'm like,

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:03.840
Am I gonna be weird?

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.590
Am I gonna say something that
they're like, "That's odd."

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:07.460
(laughter)

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.760
I didn't know the format.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:09.593
- It builds character.

00:01:09.593 --> 00:01:10.426
They'll be fine.

00:01:10.426 --> 00:01:11.770
- I come out in a wig.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.030
When we kind of started messing,

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:15.150
because we really changed the format.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.633
I'm like, I want it
less performance driven

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.673
and more, what are these kids up to?

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:24.460
They're just doing things,

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.323
and they're so in their own
skin at such an early age.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.453
I just think there's so much.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:35.370
People get so much attention
for really being cruel.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.840
And then you have kids like Ella

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.030
who's the kid governor for Connecticut.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.150
She's so funny.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.640
She's exactly like her 11
year old self in a kid.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.290
Look at that face!

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:47.123
She's so cute.

00:01:47.123 --> 00:01:48.076
- [Kelly] Look at the eye brows.

00:01:48.076 --> 00:01:48.909
I love it.

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:49.742
- [Melissa] She's such a riot.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.575
- [Kelly] Just attitude.

00:01:50.575 --> 00:01:54.407
She goes, "I want my
kids to read about hatred

00:01:54.407 --> 00:01:58.757
"and what homophobia is in the textbooks

00:01:58.757 --> 00:02:01.677
"because I want them to
not know what it is."

00:02:01.677 --> 00:02:04.670
And I was just like, "I'm sorry, what?"

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.887
She's like, "I want them
to read about it in history

00:02:06.887 --> 00:02:08.767
"and for me to have to explain it to them.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:10.410
"That's what my goal is."

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.751
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:02:11.751 --> 00:02:14.001
(applause)

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:18.290
- All these kids have so many,

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:22.118
their heart is so big, and
their conviction's so strong.

00:02:22.118 --> 00:02:25.470
It's a big thing at any
age to just be like,

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.200
I know it's not what everybody's doing,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.360
but I'm okay with it.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.250
- To see the world through
their eyes would be wonderful.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.130
If we could just stop and slow down.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.423
- I would like just a non aerosol spray.

00:02:40.098 --> 00:02:42.100
I would love to just be
like, "You seem mean."

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.813
Like just spray you with a seven year old.

00:02:43.813 --> 00:02:44.646
(laughter)

00:02:44.646 --> 00:02:47.047
If I cold bottle that and just
run arounds spraying people.

00:02:47.047 --> 00:02:48.743
Somehow that clip will be taken out

00:02:48.743 --> 00:02:51.930
and will seem very weird later.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.495
Just talk about macing people.

00:02:53.495 --> 00:02:54.328
(laughter)

00:02:54.328 --> 00:02:55.870
- You're a turd.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.780
- That seemed better before I said it.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.820
I seem like a real weirdo now.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:01.940
- You gotta bring humor into it,

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.780
and I think that's why they
obviously wanted you too

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.900
because you have a very great heart,

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.120
but you're also very
humorous and you have kids.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.240
Speaking of your kids,
are they little big shots?

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.130
Do they do stuff that really shock you?

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.453
- They shock me a lot.

00:03:16.488 --> 00:03:19.230
They're perfectly weird and funny

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.393
in the best way.

00:03:20.393 --> 00:03:21.226
- So they're you.

00:03:21.226 --> 00:03:22.059
(laughter)

00:03:22.059 --> 00:03:25.030
- Between me, Ben, my husband,
is much quieter and mellower,

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.240
but he's super weird.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.860
I'm not gonna let him off the hook.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:30.770
Our kids are this weird
amalgamation of us.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.780
And then you really start to
see their own selves come in.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.650
So I see me.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.490
I see Ben.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:37.637
I always think, I'm like,

00:03:37.637 --> 00:03:40.240
"If I just don't screw
you up it'll be amazing."

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.970
If I had it my way I would
stuff them both in a Baby Bjorn.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:43.870
- Like a kangaroo.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:45.947
- For sure, and I'm always like,

00:03:45.947 --> 00:03:47.560
"Just sit up here."

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.420
My oldest is 12, but she's my height now.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.724
And I'm literally always like, "Come here.

00:03:52.724 --> 00:03:53.630
"Come here."

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.090
- Get on over here!

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.630
- I know, I'm like, "Get
right here on mama's lap."

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.603
She's like, "That's just odd.

00:03:58.603 --> 00:04:00.127
"I'm wearing your shoes.

00:04:00.127 --> 00:04:01.633
"I don't want to sit on your lap."

00:04:01.633 --> 00:04:02.466
(laughter)

00:04:02.466 --> 00:04:03.299
- Rude.

00:04:03.299 --> 00:04:04.132
(cheering)

00:04:04.132 --> 00:04:06.635
It's All the Feels February on this show.

00:04:06.635 --> 00:04:07.468
- Oh, all the feels.

00:04:07.468 --> 00:04:09.430
- And nothing gives us all the feels

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.300
like our families and friends.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.330
So if you're up for it,

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:15.090
I'd love to scroll through your Instagram

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:16.280
'cause you've got a great Instagram.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.980
I want to meet some of
your family and friends.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:18.813
Is that cool?

00:04:18.813 --> 00:04:19.646
- Sure.

00:04:19.646 --> 00:04:20.479
I'm like, "What is it?"

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.173
- Here we go.

00:04:22.173 --> 00:04:23.006
Let's see the first one.

00:04:23.006 --> 00:04:24.880
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.070
That is a long time ago.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.830
We look like kids in that.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.370
- [Kelly] So wait, explain this to us.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.263
- I think that Ben and I, oh god.

00:04:34.263 --> 00:04:36.920
I bet we had just,

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.840
we might have been at
Groundlings, the improv theatre.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:40.750
- [Kelly] What a great place to meet.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.013
- We met in class.

00:04:44.537 --> 00:04:47.500
We were both still in our 20's for sure.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:48.650
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.328
- I look at that I'm like,
"Look at how hopeful we were."

00:04:51.328 --> 00:04:53.030
(laughter)

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:53.863
- That's what hope looked like.

00:04:53.863 --> 00:04:54.713
- Full of energy,

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.270
sleeping full through nights.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.300
It's wonderful.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.570
- [Kelly] Who needs that?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.403
- Oh my god.

00:05:00.403 --> 00:05:01.236
- What's next?

00:05:01.236 --> 00:05:02.280
Let's see the next one?

00:05:03.117 --> 00:05:04.018
(laughter)

00:05:04.018 --> 00:05:05.450
- Oh god.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.490
I'd like to explain.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.570
(laughter)

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.560
Sadly, I'd like to say
the one with the tiny hat,

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.993
which by the way was
from Barbie Western Wear.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.750
I'd love to say it was
a joke or a character.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.850
It wasn't.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:21.420
I was told when I got to LA

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.620
because I had only done plays in New York.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:27.887
I finally was like, "I'm
getting a commercial agent."

00:05:27.887 --> 00:05:30.290
I wasn't, but I was going
to meet with someone.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.257
And he said, "If you
want to work in this town

00:05:32.257 --> 00:05:34.040
"you've got to do character shots",

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:38.200
and I was like, "Oh I think
those make me uncomfortable."

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.237
I said, "Is that when
someone's in a cop jacket

00:05:40.237 --> 00:05:41.810
"and the next thing they're the burglar?"

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.240
I was like, "I don't
think I want to do that."

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.677
And he's like, "Well then
you don't want to work,

00:05:45.677 --> 00:05:47.480
"and you can't work with me."

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.170
I didn't know it was supposed to be like

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:54.020
things you may get cast as
like a waitress or a cop.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.387
So I went to do that
headshot and I was like,

00:05:56.387 --> 00:05:57.597
"This is Carol.

00:05:57.597 --> 00:05:59.441
"She works at a Vaughan's."

00:05:59.441 --> 00:06:00.712
(laughter)

00:06:00.712 --> 00:06:01.880
What you can't see is

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.870
under the picture I'm
holding a plastic tray

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.720
with Velveeta slices on it.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:07.720
(laughter)

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:08.777
And I had a whole thing I was like,

00:06:08.777 --> 00:06:11.097
"She works in a grocery
store at the end of an aisle,

00:06:11.097 --> 00:06:12.970
"and she passes out cheese samples."

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.416
- [Kelly] She's about
to whip up some Rotel.

00:06:14.416 --> 00:06:17.522
- I brought that back to
my agent and he was like,

00:06:17.522 --> 00:06:18.926
"What the hell is this?"

00:06:18.926 --> 00:06:19.940
(laughter)

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.660
He's like, "What does
this mean to anyone?"

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:22.722
I'm like, "I don't know.

00:06:22.722 --> 00:06:23.956
"I said I didn't want to do it."

00:06:23.956 --> 00:06:24.789
- It stands out.

00:06:24.789 --> 00:06:26.400
- It sure did.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.560
No one ever calls me in on that

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:29.700
because I look crazy.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.580
- Their loss.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:31.910
That's what I say.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:32.743
Next.

00:06:32.743 --> 00:06:34.340
(cheering)

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.954
- Can you always speak on my behalf?

00:06:35.954 --> 00:06:37.640
(laughter)

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.100
Oh that's my mom.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.259
- [Kelly] That's awesome.

00:06:40.259 --> 00:06:43.734
- I think we were at the Oscar's luncheon.

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:44.567
(applause)

00:06:44.567 --> 00:06:45.400
That's my mom.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.110
- You're at the Oscar's luncheon?

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.730
What's the Oscar's luncheon?

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:51.706
- It's like a fever dream.

00:06:51.706 --> 00:06:53.137
You show up and you're just like,

00:06:53.137 --> 00:06:55.135
"Someone's gonna ask me
to leave in a minute."

00:06:55.135 --> 00:06:56.990
(laughter)

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:59.340
If you're nominated there's
an Oscar's luncheon,

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:03.100
and you go and it's
just the nominees there.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.310
You can bring a date, and
I brought my mom Sandy.

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:06.350
- That's awesome.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:07.380
Hey Sandy.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.023
Okay, next.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:12.340
Oh god I love the hair.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:15.050
- Just permed, so many perms back then.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:15.883
- [Kelly] So many perms.

00:07:15.883 --> 00:07:17.750
- That's my sister Margie.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.300
I bet I'm in grade school
maybe she's in high school,

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.470
and we just did lots of perms

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:25.455
and then just so much All
Net and a curling iron.

00:07:25.455 --> 00:07:26.755
- Oh my god the Aqua Net and
you'd hold it out with a dryer.

00:07:26.755 --> 00:07:29.431
- Crispy, crispy, open,
(clicks tongue) ringlet.

00:07:29.431 --> 00:07:31.540
And then sometimes you'd only get to here

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:33.241
and you'd get tired.

00:07:33.241 --> 00:07:35.510
I'd have all these huge ringlets

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.157
and the back was just like (moans).

00:07:38.102 --> 00:07:40.480
- Like you got a little
version of a mullet hair cut.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.200
- Yeah that was down time hair.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.800
If we were going out it was like...

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:45.967
- That's so Texan.

00:07:45.967 --> 00:07:47.573
Okay next.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.070
Oh my gosh I love this.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.239
- You know you make some
choices sometimes that are...

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:56.302
- [Kelly] It's a nice denim choice.

00:07:56.302 --> 00:07:58.027
- I think my mom and dad were like,

00:07:58.027 --> 00:08:00.829
"We want to have nice
pictures of you girls taken."

00:08:00.829 --> 00:08:02.091
- I think it's awesome.

00:08:02.091 --> 00:08:03.197
- For some reason Margie and I were like,

00:08:03.197 --> 00:08:05.700
"We should wear matching denim shirts

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:09.410
and do like the cop poster back to back."

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:10.243
- I love it.

00:08:10.243 --> 00:08:11.449
It's very Charlie's Angels.

00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:12.373
- Sure.

00:08:13.477 --> 00:08:16.263
Without any of the coolness.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.080
- I love denim girl.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:18.913
You're talkin' to a Texan.

00:08:18.913 --> 00:08:20.276
- I love denim,

00:08:20.276 --> 00:08:22.563
but just somehow we've
gone off the mark on that.

00:08:22.563 --> 00:08:23.797
(laughter)

00:08:23.797 --> 00:08:24.630
- You did not.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:25.463
Next.

00:08:25.463 --> 00:08:26.520
Let's see the next one.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.702
Oh my gosh they're little lions.

00:08:28.702 --> 00:08:29.785
- They are.

00:08:29.785 --> 00:08:32.800
That's still Harper and Homer.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.633
- They're Golden Retrievers?

00:08:33.633 --> 00:08:34.650
- They're Golden Retrievers,

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:37.430
and I got these Amazon lion things.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:38.470
And when they showed up

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:40.930
they're made of just old syringes.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:41.898
They're terrible,

00:08:41.898 --> 00:08:44.148
(laughter)

00:08:48.281 --> 00:08:51.080
but they were the exact
same colors as my dogs.

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:53.200
So I put them on I was
out in the back yard

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:57.120
trying to get two crazy one
year old dogs to sit still.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.090
And then he yawned and I'm like, "Yep.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:00.065
- Yep.

00:09:00.065 --> 00:09:00.898
(laughter)

00:09:00.898 --> 00:09:01.731
But it looks like a (roars)

00:09:01.731 --> 00:09:02.564
- They never went on again.

00:09:02.564 --> 00:09:03.397
They truly look like lions.

00:09:03.397 --> 00:09:04.710
- I love it.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:05.543
I love it.

00:09:05.543 --> 00:09:07.097
The old syringe look.

00:09:07.097 --> 00:09:07.930
(laughter)

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:09.810
Alright one more, we've got one more.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:11.270
Oh my god, you're dying.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.340
You're laughing.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:13.680
Wait, what's happening?

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:14.920
- Oh my god I don't
remember putting that on.

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:18.080
That is two of my dearest
friends in the world.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.260
It's Brian Atwood, who's
a fantastic shoe designer,

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.480
and then Michael McGraw.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:25.360
I went to high school with Brian,

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.270
Michael I met on the dance
floor of the Palladium

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:30.230
in the '90s.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.647
And I marched up to him and said,

00:09:31.647 --> 00:09:34.357
"That's the ugliest jacket I've ever seen.

00:09:34.357 --> 00:09:36.030
"I love it."

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.540
And we have never been apart since.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:38.373
- Oh my god.

00:09:38.373 --> 00:09:40.475
- That was us in Vegas.

00:09:40.475 --> 00:09:43.096
- Do you remember what you're laughing at?

00:09:43.096 --> 00:09:45.240
Or is it not daytime worthy?

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.340
- It's for sure not daytime worthy.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.960
I can't remember,

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:52.427
but that is probably what we
look like 90% of the time.

00:09:52.427 --> 00:09:55.302
- [Kelly] Those are great friends.

00:09:55.302 --> 00:09:56.135
You need to laugh.

00:09:56.135 --> 00:09:57.370
- [Melissa] They were both
my bridesmen for my wedding.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.870
- Oh my gosh that's awesome.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.617
I hope you asked him to wear the jacket.

00:10:01.617 --> 00:10:03.560
(laughter)

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:04.585
Just wear that number.

00:10:04.585 --> 00:10:05.871
- Just wear it, come one.

